  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important first step is to establish a clean, minimal baseline that isolates the RNA signal without confounding factors from image modality, complex encoders, multiprofile aggregation, or fusion. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: a linear PCA reduction of the RNA profile with no additional architectural complexity. This gives a reference accuracy/F1 against which all subsequent experiments (stronger RNA encoders like scvi/scgpt, image-only models, multimodal fusion, multiprofile aggregation) can be meaningfully compared. Establishing this floor first reduces uncertainty about whether the task is solvable at all and how much headroom more complex designs might offer, making the remaining 9 experiments far more informative."
}

